@@ -0,0 +1,58 @@
+---
+id: fix/cant-make-change
+title: The drawer cannot make change
+parent: fix
+summary: Respond when the cash drawer ledger cannot make exact change, or check whether a different handover would work.
+tags: [cash, change, drawer, ledger, notes, coins, part payment, cash rounding]
+related: [fix, cash/change, cash/check-change, pay/cash]
+updated: 2026-10-11
+---
+If the Cash sheet says it **Can't make … change**, the notes and coins recorded in the drawer cannot make that exact amount from the handover and current ledger. Review the displayed options before taking the cash.
+
+## Basic
+
+### Choose an offered option
+The sheet may offer:
+- **Use that smaller handover**: accept a smaller set of the notes the customer gave, return the rest, and make the change from the drawer.
+- **Cash … + the rest another way**: take the displayed amount in cash and collect the remaining balance by card or another tender.
+- Take the full amount by card.
+
+If the ledger is empty or out of date, count the drawer and correct the ledger first. You can use **The drawer has it (ledger is out of date)** only when you have physically checked that the drawer can provide the displayed change.
+
+### If you have already taken the cash
+In **Give change**, the POS suggests notes and coins if it finds an exact combination. Check what you actually hand over, then tap **Gave this**. If needed, choose different denominations manually. You can choose **Done, but don't track it** if you do not want to record the notes and coins.
+
+For the normal cash flow and denominations, see [[pay/cash]] and [[cash/change]].
+
+## Deep
+
+### Ledger count versus physical drawer
+The suggestion uses the ledger's note and coin counts plus the notes the customer just handed over. If the actual drawer differs from the ledger, the suggestion can be impossible or not match the physical cash. Count or correct the ledger before relying on a suggestion.
+
+The override is a manual acknowledgement that the physical drawer can make the change despite the ledger. The **Give change** step records what was actually handed over when denominations are confirmed; choosing not to track leaves that cash out of the drawer record.
+
+### Do not promise change the drawer cannot make
+The POS blocks the normal overpayment path when it cannot make exact change. Ask for a different handover, use the suggested part-cash option, or use another tender. If the customer gives the exact amount, you can take it without tracking denominations.
+
+## Advanced
+
+### Change decision
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+  A[Tap received notes and coins] --> B{Amount covers cash due}
+  B -->|no| C[Ask for more or take part payment]
+  B -->|yes exact| D[Take cash]
+  B -->|over| E{Drawer plus handover makes exact change}
+  E -->|yes| F[Review and confirm notes given]
+  E -->|no| G[Offer smaller handover part cash or card]
+  G --> H[Override only after physical drawer check]
+```
+
+| Job | Where |
+|---|---|
+| Cash sheet prompts and handover options | `src/screens/CashSheet.tsx` |
+| Cash amount states, exact-change plan and fallback choices | `cashStatus`, `planChange`, `handBackOptions`, `partCashOption` in `src/lib/cashSale.ts` |
+| Note and coin counts | `src/lib/cashLedger.ts`, `src/ui/DenomPad.tsx` |
+| Check Change tool | `src/lib/checkChange.ts`, `src/screens/CheckChange.tsx` |
+
+The hardware tender machine is not active. The cashier enters received and given denominations and confirms them manually.
diff --git a/help/fix/stock-mismatch.md b/help/fix/stock-mismatch.md
new file mode 100644
index 0000000..3929504
--- /dev/null
+++ b/help/fix/stock-mismatch.md
@@ -0,0 +1,55 @@
+---
+id: fix/stock-mismatch
+title: Stock counts differ from Shopify
+parent: fix
+summary: Refresh the selected location's stock, check variant tracking and distinguish local sales from Shopify's available quantity.
+tags: [stock, inventory, mismatch, Shopify, location, tracked, refresh, negative]
+related: [fix, stock, stock/inventory, settings/shopify]
+updated: 2026-10-11
+---
+Inventory shows stock for the Shopify location selected on this register. Refresh from Shopify before comparing, and make sure you are looking at the same location and variant in both places.
+
+## Basic
+
+### Refresh the catalogue and stock
+1. Check the location in **More ▸ Settings ▸ Shopify**.
+2. Open **Inventory** and tap **Refresh stock from Shopify**.
+3. In **Filters & sort**, check the import time and total variants on this iPad.
+4. Search by variant name, SKU or barcode and check that the product status and stock filters do not hide it.
+
+If this register is connected to the wrong location, select the correct active location and refresh again. For the filter meanings and stock update controls, see [[stock/inventory]].
+
+### Check whether the item is tracked
+**—** means inventory is not tracked; **0** means tracked and currently out of stock. A negative number means more units have been sold than the available count. Check the tracked setting and available quantity for that exact variant in Shopify.
+
+## Deep
+
+### Why registers can temporarily differ
+Shopify is the shared source. Each register keeps a local catalogue and stock snapshot. Sales update this register's local count immediately, while the sale upload and the other registers' stock refresh happen separately. A register that is offline or has not polled yet can show an older count.
+
+The POS reads the selected location's **available** quantity. Shopify's other inventory states or another location may not match that number.
+
+### When a sale is queued
+A completed sale reduces the local count and queues its Shopify order. If it is still queued, correct the sync issue rather than adjusting stock to make the local display look right. See [[fix/offline-sync]].
+
+## Advanced
+
+### Stock update and refresh path
+```mermaid
+flowchart TD
+  A[Choose active Shopify location] --> B[Import variants and available quantity]
+  B --> C[Save local catalogue snapshot]
+  D[Complete a sale] --> E[Reduce local stock]
+  E --> F[Upload order to Shopify]
+  F --> G[Other registers refresh stock delta]
+```
+
+| Job | Where |
+|---|---|
+| Select location and full catalogue import | `src/screens/Settings.tsx`, `importFromShopify` in `src/lib/sync.ts` |
+| Read tracked and available stock | `fetchVariants` in `src/lib/shopify/catalogue.ts` |
+| Poll location stock changes | `fetchStockDelta` in `src/lib/shopify/catalogue.ts`, `pollShared` in `src/lib/sync.ts` |
+| Mirror completed sale stock locally | `applyLocalStock` in `src/lib/sync.ts` |
+| Set or adjust stock from the POS | `src/screens/Inventory.tsx`, `src/lib/shopify/inventory.ts` |
+
+Compare the same variant, location and Shopify quantity name (**available**). A manual Inventory count or adjustment writes to Shopify; do not use one to conceal a delayed sync.
